answer":"Based on the given passages, here's how a flat screen TV works:

Flat screen TVs use either plasma or LCD technology to produce images. In a plasma TV, cells containing xenon and neon gases are sandwiched between two sheets of glass. Electrodes are arranged in a grid pattern on either side of the cells, and when an electric pulse is applied, the gases produce ultraviolet photons that react with phosphor material to produce light. In an LCD TV, tiny liquid-crystal-filled cells are used instead of plasma cells. A bright white light behind the cells illuminates them to create the image.

So, in summary, flat screen TVs work by using electricity to excite gases or liquids, which then produce light to create the images on the screen.","source_segments":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":35},{"index":1,"byte_start":35,"byte_end":125},{"index":2,"byte_start":125,"byte_end":199},{"index":3,"byte_start":199,"byte_end":497},{"index":4,"byte_start":497,"byte_end":680},{"index":5,"byte_start":680,"byte_end":725},{"index":6,"byte_start":725,"byte_end":779},{"index":7,"byte_start":779,"byte_end":812},{"index":8,"byte_start":812,"byte_end":965},{"index":9,"byte_start":965,"byte_end":1076},{"index":10,"byte_start":1076,"byte_end":1131},{"index":11,"byte_start":1131,"byte_end":1238},{"index":12,"byte_start":1238,"byte_end":1322},{"index":13,"byte_start":1322,"byte_end":1415},{"index":14,"byte_start":1415,"byte_end":1494},{"index":15,"byte_start":1494,"byte_end":1614},{"index":16,"byte_start":1614,"byte_end":1756}],"answer_sentence_indices":[0,1,2,3,4,5],"answer_offsets":[{"index":0,"byte_start":0,"byte_end":136},{"index":1,"byte_start":136,"byte_end":234},{"index":2,"byte_start":234,"byte_end":434},{"index":3,"byte_start":434,"byte_end":515},{"index":4,"byte_start":515,"byte_end":592},{"index":5,"byte_start":592,"byte_end":738}]}

